  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "Herbert Gallen was an American fashion entrepreneur who founded Ellen Tracy and built it into a major women’s clothing label. Starting with blouses, he broadened the company under designer Linda Allard into coordinated sportswear and professional fashion. Long-term creative consistency and department-store distribution made the brand valuable enough for an eventual sale to Liz Claiborne.",
